            <div class="diptych-text">
              <p class="diptych-suptitle">Star Wars trivia</p>
              <h2 class="title2">Andor Q&amp;A</h2>
              <div class="accordion">
                <details
                  class="accordion-item"
                  name="questions-answers"
                  open>
                  <summary class="accordion-title">
                    How were most Andor scenes shot ?
                  </summary>
                  <div class="accordion-content">
                    <p>
                      Andor establishes each scene in the series by giving
                      priority to the real elements. While other Star Wars shows
                      start with a wide shot making heavy use of CGI, Andor
                      focuses on tangible elements and makes use of vast sets
                      built in the real world.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>
                <details
                  class="accordion-item"
                  name="questions-answers">
                  <summary class="accordion-title">
                    What is Andor's timeline ?
                  </summary>
                  <div class="accordion-content">
                    <p>
                      The events in Andor (apart from the flashbacks on Kenari)
                      happen in the five years before Rogue One. They describe
                      the journey of Cassion Andor to becoming a ruthless
                      rebellion operative. The first season documents the first
                      year of that journey, while each three episodes arc of
                      season two covers roughly one year.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>
                <details
                  class="accordion-item"
                  name="questions-answers">
                  <summary class="accordion-title">
                    How well was Andor recieved ?
                  </summary>
                  <div class="accordion-content">
                    <p>
                      Both seasons of Andor were very well recieved. Critics and
                      viewers hailed its mature and political take on the Star
                      Wars universe. The first season was considered one the
                      best series of 2022, while its second season climed to the
                      top of the charts in 2025.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>
                <details
                  class="accordion-item"
                  name="questions-answers">
                  <summary class="accordion-title">
                    What is the show's main theme ?
                  </summary>
                  <div class="accordion-content">
                    <p>
                      Gilroy wanted to propose a gritty view of what it takes to
                      organize a rebellion against a tyrannical government set
                      on centralizing control and normalizing mass surveillance.
                      Instead of Jedis, lightsabers and the force, Andor focuses
                      on the choices ordinary people are forced to make when
                      confronted with fascism and authoritarism.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </div>
